# 15 — Unity Export

> **For the agent reading this:** Read `plans/thinking-08-unity-export.md` first. It holds Orlando's notes: why a level designed in orlablocks should reach Unity, the two options weighed (bake everything into one file, or rebuild the scene in Unity), and the flow Orlando wants: design to 90% in orlablocks, play it in Unity, keep working there, and refresh from orlablocks when a part needs redesigning. Background: `plans/07-geometry-tools` (holes, taper and bevel, tilt), `plans/08-semantics-and-entities` (tags, entities and instances), `plans/10-array-tools` (arrays and their items), `plans/14-real-work-improvements` (scale and tilt on instances and arrays).
>
> The phase takes Option 2's flow with one change: **Unity doesn't rebuild the geometry.** orlablocks bakes every mesh (holes cut, normals and UVs as the editor draws them), and Unity owns the structure: one GameObject per node, entities as prefabs, a refresh matched by node ID, and mappings kept in Unity. It has two halves:
> - **orlablocks side:** the bake moves to `src/shared/` so the editor and the export draw the same thing, then an **export** writes a scene to a folder (a manifest and a binary of meshes), from the editor, the agent (`export_scene`) or on every step;
> - **Unity side:** C# files (runtime components, editor code) that Orlando copies into a Unity 6 (6000.5) URP project to test. They're written so they can become a package later, which Orlando will make and add to this repo. **No package is made in this phase:** no `package.json`, no UPM setup.
>
> The work is split into small increments (§12). Each orlablocks increment ends with `npm test` and `npm run typecheck` passing and a scripted check against a spare server (`PORT=5171 DATA_DIR=<scratch>`). Each Unity increment ends with a checklist for Orlando, who imports the files into their project. The server's MCP version goes up one patch per increment that changes it, starting from 0.0.38. Add this phase's terms to `GLOSSARY.md` (marked "from 15") as they land. Log progress in §16 at the end of this file.

