## 8. Notes, lines and ProBuilder (15.6)

- **Notes:** `Gizmos.cs` draws a flag at the pin with its label and color, and the text as a `Handles.Label` when selected or when the Level's **Show notes** is on. Done notes are faint. `EditorOnly`.
- **Lines:** a polyline gizmo in the line's color (dashed and arrow as in orlablocks), with `OrlaLine.points` public so a tool can read a route (the race line) in the editor. `EditorOnly` by default. A tag mapping can keep one in builds, e.g. `#route` → not EditorOnly.
- **Claim as ProBuilder:** with `com.unity.probuilder` installed (the editor asmdef's `versionDefines` sets `ORLA_PROBUILDER`), a node's context menu converts its body mesh to a `ProBuilderMesh`, keeping materials. The node is then claimed. Without ProBuilder, the menu item doesn't exist.
- **Lightmap UVs:** a Level option generates UV2 (`Unwrapping.GenerateSecondaryUVSet`) on rebuilt meshes. Off by default because it's slow.

---

## 9. Mappings (15.5)

`OrlaMappings` is a ScriptableObject that the Level points at. One can serve several levels of a project.

- **Entities:** entity ID (picked from the last export's entities, shown by name) → a prefab, with `scale` (× the instance's, default 1) and `blockout`:
  - `replace` (the default): the mapped prefab only;
  - `keep hidden`: the generated prefab as a disabled child, to compare;
  - `keep`.
  The mapped prefab's root gets an `OrlaNode`, so matching (§7) works the same. Changing a mapping swaps the instances on the next sync, keeping the user's additions under them (moved to the new instance).
- **Tags:** tag → any of a layer, a Unity tag, components (script types, picked as `MonoScript`s, stored as type names), static flags, and **keep in builds** (for lines). Applied to the tagged node and, for a group, to what's under it. Added components are the user's after that: a sync adds them if missing and never removes them.
- **Colors:** palette key → body material and floor material, instead of the generated ones.
- A missing mapped prefab or script is reported and falls back to the generated one.

---

## 10. Everyday use

- **One Level per orlablocks scene.** A Unity scene can hold several Levels (the agent's version next to Orlando's, from 14.5). Entities of one project share generated prefabs.
- **Moving a level in Unity:** move the Level's own GameObject. Its children are synced in its local space, so this isn't drift.
- **Continuing in Unity** (Orlando's "work just continues in Unity"): claim what's being worked on, or stop syncing (**Auto sync** off). **Disconnect** removes every `OrlaNode` and leaves plain GameObjects and prefab instances.

---

## 11. Risks

- **Prefab overrides on items:** a cut item overrides one child's mesh. If an entity's definition later drops that shape, the override is dead. Sync clears overrides it no longer needs.
- **Big levels:** thousands of GameObjects. Measure on the flight level; the fallback is the merging deferred in §2.
- **Export on every step during a fast drag:** the export waits for the step to finish and debounces 1 s, and the watcher throttles in Unity.
- **The bake refactor could change what the editor draws.** `useShapeGeometry`'s output is compared before and after in a unit test (same vertices, normals, UVs) for each shape type.

